tyle="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 1pt 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">EVE</span></td><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">11.72&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">%</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">7.36&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">%</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 1pt 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">N/A</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">(4.78&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">%)</span></td><td colspan="3" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:0 1pt"/><td colspan="2" style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 0 1.5pt 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">(9.81&#160;</span></td><td style="background-color:#ccffcc;padding:2.62pt 1pt 1.5pt 0;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:9pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">%)</span></td></tr></table></div><div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"><span><br/></span></div><div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">To supplement the instantaneous rate shocks required by regulatory guidance, we also calculate our interest rate risk position assuming a gradual change in market interest rates. This gradual change is commonly referred to as a &#8220;rate ramp&#8221; and evenly allocates a change in interest rates over a specified time period.</span></div><div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"><span><br/></span></div><div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Presented below is the estimated impact on the Company&#8217;s NII and EVE position as of June&#160;30, 2026, assuming a static balance sheet and gradual parallel shifts in interest rates:</span></div><div style="text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt"><span><br/></span></div><div style="margin-bottom:1pt;margin-top:5pt;text-align:justify"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:100.000%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"/><td style="width:17.015%"/><td style="width:0.1%"/><td s